    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">Live product reference · Observed 13 November 2026</p>
      <h1>The three launched Nirantar sevas</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Actual offering and temple images from jaibhakti.com, with its displayed
        names, weekly schedule and introductory/regular amounts. The colors,
        wordmark and typography follow the original final design.
      </p>
      <div class="catalogue-cards">{{OFFERING_CARDS}}</div>
      <section class="context-panel">
        <h2>How this connects to the design</h2>
        <div class="flow-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Web: take the booking</h3>
            <p>
              Identify the actual offering and temple, show the purchased terms
              and beneficiary, and confirm payment from the authoritative
              service.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>App: follow the booking</h3>
            <p>
              Show ongoing bookings, registered dates, performed dates and
              independently ready certificates/videos. Book More must preserve
              the selected offering.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Shared product rules</h3>
            <p>
              Keep product/package identity and purchased price snapshots
              consistent. Account holder, payer and beneficiary are separate
              concepts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <p class="notice">
        <strong>Open decisions remain.</strong> The live pages display automatic
        renewal/cancellation wording alongside a promise referring to a selected
        number of weeks. Actual mandate duration and later authorization remain
        to be confirmed. These observed prices are references, not a newly
        approved payment contract.
      </p>
      <p class="hint">
        The app draft still contains illustrative products and bookings,
        including Hanuman. Those samples do not establish another launched
        offer. The catalogue above records the three live offers; later
        purchases must use confirmed IDs and terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="../walkthroughs/index.html#app/0"
          >Review the proposed app journey →</a
        >
        ·
        <a href="../docs/08_Live_Seva_Catalogue.md"
          >Read the asset provenance and mapping →</a
        >
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
